Done. Here's what was implemented:

**`logfan.go`** — two types:

- **`Ring`** — ring-buffer `slog.Handler` with O(1) insert/evict. Stores `preAttrs` from `WithAttrs()` and applies them during `Handle()`. `Records()` returns a deep copy (mutating the result doesn't touch the buffer). Thread-safe via `sync.RWMutex`.
- **`multiHandler`** — fans every record to all registered handlers; `New()` wraps it into an `*slog.Logger`.

**`logfan_test.go`** — 20 tests covering:

| Area | Tests |
|---|---|
| `NewRing` validation | invalid capacity (0, -1), empty ring |
| Ring store/retrieve | single record, oldest-first ordering, eviction (past capacity and multi-wraparound), exact capacity, levels, timestamps |
| Deep copy | mutating returned slice doesn't affect ring |
| Concurrency | 20 writers + 10 readers |
| slog integration | `Enabled`, direct `slog.New()`, `With("key","val")` attrs flow through handler |
| fan-out `New()` | zero-handler error, fan-out to 2 rings, fan-out with attrs |
| `WithAttrs` / `WithGroup` | returned Ring works and stores records correctly |
